  {
   "name": "bbbc006_u2os_hoechst_zstack",
   "kind": "focus",
   "description": "Widefield fluorescence z-stack of U2OS cell nuclei (Hoechst 33342, channel w1), well A02 site 1, 20x/0.45 NA, 696x520 16-bit grayscale TIFF (LZW). 34 planes z=00..33 at 2 um spacing; dataset says z=16 is optimal focus and z=11..23 are in focus. Direction (above/below) of low vs high z is not stated unambiguously. Files are only distributed inside one ~800 MB zip per z-plane; each slice can be fetched alone with HTTP range requests (offsets given), or use the local copies. Suggested small test subset: z=08,10,...,24 (9 planes, flag recommended_subset). Matching phalloidin channel (w2) for the same field was also extracted locally. Note: a flat monolayer, so the 'all in focus' result is close to the z=16 slice; good for testing sharpness selection and 16-bit handling, less for depth extension.",
   "licence": "CC0: dataset page states 'To the extent possible under law, Anne Carpenter has waived all copyright and related or neighboring rights to out-of-focus U2OS images and ground truth. This work is published from: United States.'",
